### Actor Access Provenance (INVARIANT — cmps.6)
The actor access provenance block in the Actor Profile section is **authoritative**.  If the pinned entry point has INDIRECT controllability, the actor MUST provide structured influence evidence (influence_source, influence_mechanism, trust_boundary_id) — the narrative must not contradict this evidence.  No blanket actor-type allowlist determines indirect eligibility; the structured evidence does.  If advisory kill-chain wording conflicts with the access provenance block, the access provenance block wins.

Do NOT invent upload portals, merchant dashboards, partner repositories, or write-access mechanisms for indirect-controllability entry points unless the actor access provenance includes structured influence evidence.  If the narrative requires the attacker to modify data in an indirect entry point, the actor access provenance MUST include influence_source, influence_mechanism, and trust_boundary_id.

